      "worked": "Let the diagonals meet at $O$, and let $A$ denote the quadrilateral's area. The four angles at $O$ are $\\theta$ or $180^\\circ-\\theta$. Since $\\sin(180^\\circ-\\theta)=\\sin\\theta$, the triangle area rule gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\nA&=\\operatorname{Area}(\\triangle AOB)+\\operatorname{Area}(\\triangle BOC)+\\operatorname{Area}(\\triangle COD)+\\operatorname{Area}(\\triangle DOA)\\\\\nA&=\\frac12\\bigl(AO\\cdot BO+BO\\cdot CO+CO\\cdot DO+DO\\cdot AO\\bigr)\\sin\\theta\\\\\nA&=\\frac12(AO+CO)(BO+DO)\\sin\\theta\\\\\nA&=\\frac12(AC)(BD)\\sin\\theta.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
